    {
      "@id": "skills/authoring/authoring-core/voice-editorial-review.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The scoping question comes first, and it is usually the answer",
      "prov:value": "None of them carries `profiles` scoping today. So they also run over\n`docs/source/` — documentation, where the genre's whole register is to address\nthe reader: *\"you need `bun`, `latexmk` and Lean\"* is a correct sentence in a\nprerequisites page and a `voice-scholarly-default` match at the same time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/authoring/authoring-core/voice-editorial-review.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the criterion cannot know",
      "prov:value": "The checkers match text. They do not know what the page is *about*, and the\nthree highest-severity false positives in this repo all come from that:\n\n- `voice-status-leak` on `what-is-not-built-yet.md:36` — `**Not yet\n  implemented:**`. The page is a deliberate inventory of gaps; the phrase is\n  its subject, not a leak.\n- `voice-status-leak` on `how-to-read-them.md` and\n  `the-work-plan-tasks-as-beans.md` — both describe the *work-plan lane of a\n  BPMN diagram*. Prose about a to-do store contains the words of a to-do store.\n- `voice-emoji-content` in `a-mock-session.md` and `step-4-formalize-in-lean.md`\n  — the emoji sit inside a transcript of an agent session, quoted as data."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/authoring/authoring-core/voice-editorial-review.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the open findings are",
      "prov:value": "Tracked in the work plan, one bean per criterion, each carrying its blocks with\nfile, line and the matched text:\n\n```sh\nbeans list | grep \"Voice axis\"\n```"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/authoring/authoring-core/voice-editorial-review.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Do not",
      "prov:value": "- **Do not mass-apply one finding's resolution across its siblings** without\n  reading them. `voice-scholarly-default` fires ten times here on at least two\n  different causes.\n- **Do not treat `critical` as \"fix first\".** Severity ranks the criterion's\n  authors' concern, not the confidence of this match; three of the four\n  criticals in `docs/source/` are quotations."
    }
  ]
}
